cts\n\n```python\n# Feature name: log_SM6_L\n# Feature description: Log transformation of SM6_L (Spectral moment of order 6 from Laplace matrix).\n# Usefulness: Reduces skewed distribution in SM6_L, enabling the model to better capture relationships within its range.\ndf['log_SM6_L'] = np.log1p(df['SM6_L'])  # Use log1p to avoid issues with zero values\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: sqrt_SdO\n# Feature description: Square root transformation of SdO (Sum of dO E-states).\n# Usefulness: Reduces the impact of extreme or outlier values in SdO while highlighting smaller variations that may be significant for biodegradability prediction.\ndf['sqrt_SdO'] = np.sqrt(df['SdO'])\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: zscore_HyWi_B_m\n# Feature description: Z-score normalization of HyWi_B(m) (Hyper-Wiener-like index weighted by mass).\n# Usefulness: Normalizes the feature range, ensuring consistent treatment of features with varying scales in the downstream model.\ndf['zscore_HyWi_B_m'] = (df['HyWi_B(m)'] - df['HyWi_B(m)'].mean()) / df['HyWi_B(m)'].std()\n```end\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Create Binary and Categorical Features for Simplification\n\n```python\n# Feature name: binary_nN_presence\n# Feature description: Binary feature indicating whether Nitrogen atoms (nN) are present.\n# Usefulness: Nitrogen atom presence can significantly affect biodegradability, making its presence/absence a useful simplified feature.\ndf['binary_nN_presence'] = (df['nN'] > 0).astype(int)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: categorical_C_percent\n# Feature description: Categorizes C% (percentage of Carbon atoms) into quartiles.\n# Usefulness: Groups chemicals based on carbon content, capturing structural dependencies related to biodegradability.\ndf['categorical_C_percent'] = pd.qcut(df['C%'], q=4, labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High', 'Very High'])\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: binary_high_nHM\n# Feature description: Binary column indicating whether the number of heavy atoms (nHM) exceed